<div id="p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:144%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix is organized as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Pt0.A0.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS1" title="A.1 Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> gives the proof of equivalent marginal distributions between the reversed-SDE and its corresponding PF-ODE.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS2" title="A.2 Derivation of 𝒉_{𝒙_0=𝒚̃} ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> demonstrates the detailed derivation of <math id="Pt0.A0.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS3" title="A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> provides the Weighted <math id="Pt0.A0.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-Transform Inference equation for velocity-based Optimal Transport Flow Matching (OT-FM) and noise-based Variance-Preserving SDE (VP-SDE).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS4" title="A.4 Implementation details ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> indicates the implementation details of our method, including how we obtain the coarse videos, text prompts of video generation, and how we set related hyperparameters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS5" title="A.5 Additional Results ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> provides additional results, including the ablation study of weight function <math id="Pt0.A0.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and additional qualitative results.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A0.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A0.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#Pt0.A0.SS6" title="A.6 Image Editing ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> shows the extension of our method on the image editing task.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the formal proof that the stochastic differential equation (SDE) in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Guided Generation with ℎ-Transform ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and the ordinary differential equation (ODE) in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.1 Guided Generation with ℎ-Transform ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) share the same marginal distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the marginal probability density of the latent <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
We first write the drift term of the SDE (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Guided Generation with ℎ-Transform ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)) as:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-g^{2}(t)\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})-g^{2}(t){\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}(\bm{x}_{t},t)=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-g^{2}(t)\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})-g^{2}(t){\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The evolution of the probability density <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for this reverse-time SDE is governed by the Fokker-Planck equation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> (F-P equation). Taking into account the negative time increment in the reverse process, the corresponding F-P equation is given by:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}q_{t})-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\Delta q_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}q_{t})-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\Delta q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we substitute the mathematical identity <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta q_{t}=\nabla\cdot(\nabla q_{t})=\nabla\cdot(q_{t}\nabla\log q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta q_{t}=\nabla\cdot(\nabla q_{t})=\nabla\cdot(q_{t}\nabla\log q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> into Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E17" title="Equation A17 ‣ A.1 Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A17</span></a>) yields:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}q_{t})-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\cdot(q_{t}\nabla\log q_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}q_{t})-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\cdot(q_{t}\nabla\log q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We can reformulate the equation as a standard continuity equation:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot\left(\underbrace{\left[\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\log q_{t}\right]}_{\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}}q_{t}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot\left(\underbrace{\left[\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\log q_{t}\right]}_{\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}}q_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E19" title="Equation A19 ‣ A.1 Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A19</span></a>) takes the form <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial q_{t}}{\partial t}=-\nabla\cdot(\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which precisely describes the density evolution of a deterministic ODE <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\bm{x}=\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\bm{x}=\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the equivalent deterministic drift <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}</annotation></semantics></math> that shares the same marginal density <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}=\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\log q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}=\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\nabla\log q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of diffusion models, the goal of introducing the additional term <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is to shift the unconditional score to the target conditional score. By definition, the exact marginal score of the process is structurally related to the unconditional score via:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})=\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})=\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we substitute the definition of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mtext>SDE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\text{SDE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the score identity from Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E21" title="Equation A21 ‣ A.1 Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A21</span></a>) into Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E20" title="Equation A20 ‣ A.1 Equivalence Proof of Marginal Distributions ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A20</span></a>):</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A0.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-g^{2}(t)\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})-g^{2}(t){\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-g^{2}(t)\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})-g^{2}(t){\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A0.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\left(\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\left(\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Simplifying the terms, we obtain:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\left(\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C00000;" mathcolor="#C00000">𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\left(\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})+{\color[rgb]{0.7539,0,0}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{y}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">This derived drift <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mtext>ODE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{\text{ODE}}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to the drift of the ODE presented in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.1 Guided Generation with ℎ-Transform ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). Since the same continuity equation governs the probability density of the given SDE and this resulting ODE, we conclude that they exhibit the same marginal distribution <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> at all times <math id="Pt0.A0.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Derivation of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the detailed derivation of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Based on Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ 3.2 Approximation for the Untractable 𝒉_{𝒙_0=𝒚} ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), we can get the probability density function of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="Pt0.A0.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})^{d/2}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then take the <math id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math> of both sides of the equation and calculate the gradient:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="Pt0.A0.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{x_{t}}\log p_{t}(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\bm{x}_{t}}\left[-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})-\frac{\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\bm{x}_{t}}\left[-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})-\frac{\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Pt0.A0.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\nabla_{\bm{x}_{t}}\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\nabla_{\bm{x}_{t}}\|\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="Pt0.A0.E25Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{2(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{2(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="Pt0.A0.E25Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E25Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}(\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}(\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then we substitute it into Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.2 Approximation for the Untractable 𝒉_{𝒙_0=𝒚} ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and get the final <math id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒉</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒙</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#00B050;" mathcolor="#00B050">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0.6914,0.3125}\bm{h}_{\bm{x}_{0}=\widetilde{\bm{y}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="Pt0.A0.SS2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, Eq. (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.2 Approximation for the Untractable 𝒉_{𝒙_0=𝒚} ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Weighted <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-Transform Inference for Various SDEs</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derived our method, Weighted <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-Transform Inference from the Score Matching perspective in our paper, and we claim that our method is compatible with other diffusion models like DDPM and Flow Matching. In this section, we provide the derivation of the inference equation of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>-based Optimal Transport Flow Matching (OT-FM) and <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-based Variance-Preserving SDE (VP-SDE).</p>
</div>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">OT-FM with <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Flow Matching, the velocity field <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the PF-ODE drift. Thus, we have the relation:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}\quad\implies\quad\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-v_{\theta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>s</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>s</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}\quad\implies\quad\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}=\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-v_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this relation into the ODE (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.4 Weighted Approximation for Error Restriction ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>)), we rewrite the drift in terms of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A0.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>s</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{1}{2}g^{2}(t)\text{s}_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A0.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-v_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)-v_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For OT-FM, the trajectory is defined by <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=1-\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=1-\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under a linear schedule where <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=1-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=1-t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}=t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\alpha}_{t}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\alpha}_{t}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\sigma}_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\sigma}_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding drift and squared diffusion coefficients are:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A0.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A0.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}(t)=2\sigma_{t}\dot{\sigma}_{t}-2\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}=-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\sigma_{t}\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)=-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}(t)=2\sigma_{t}\dot{\sigma}_{t}-2\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\sigma_{t}^{2}=-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\sigma_{t}\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)=-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now simplify the guidance term from Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E27" title="Equation A27 ‣ OT-FM with 𝑣-prediction. ‣ A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A27</span></a>) using these coefficients:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A0.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\mathbf{f}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-2\dot{\alpha}_{t}\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A0.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}(\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}})+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A0.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{x}_{t}\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}}-\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}\right)+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{x}_{t}\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}}-\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}\right)+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Using the OT constraint <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}-1=-\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}-1=-\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the term simplifies perfectly:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{\sigma_{t}-1}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}\right)+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}=-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}=-\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{\sigma_{t}-1}{\alpha_{t}\sigma_{t}}\right)+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}=-\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}+\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}\widetilde{\bm{y}}=-\dot{\alpha}_{t}\left(\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\alpha}_{t}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\alpha}_{t}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, this term evaluates exactly to <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this back into Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E27" title="Equation A27 ‣ OT-FM with 𝑣-prediction. ‣ A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A27</span></a>) yields the final velocity-based guided ODE:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}-v_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\left[v_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}-v_{\theta}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">VP-SDE with <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-Prediction.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a VP forward process <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\bm{x}_{0}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\bm{x}_{0}+\sigma_{t}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> constrained by <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{2}+\sigma_{t}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{2}+\sigma_{t}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the drift and diffusion coefficients are also uniquely determined by the schedule <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E28" title="Equation A28 ‣ OT-FM with 𝑣-prediction. ‣ A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A28</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E29" title="Equation A29 ‣ OT-FM with 𝑣-prediction. ‣ A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A29</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-prediction framework, the score function is parameterized as <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{s}_{\theta}=-\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>s</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{s}_{\theta}=-\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{s}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>s</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{s}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> into Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 3.4 Weighted Approximation for Error Restriction ‣ 3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), we obtain:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A0.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}\left(-2\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)\left(-\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}+\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{1}{2}\left(-2\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\right)\left(-\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}+\frac{\epsilon_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A0.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A0.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left[\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}}\left(\epsilon_{\theta}-\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}+\epsilon_{\theta}\right)\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left[\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}}\left(\epsilon_{\theta}-\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}+\epsilon_{\theta}\right)\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We define the pseudo-target noise corresponding to the condition <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}=\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}=\frac{\bm{x}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}}{\sigma_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By observing that <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}=-\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha_{t}\widetilde{\bm{y}}-\bm{x}_{t}}{\sigma_{t}}=-\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can substitute this into the inner guidance term in Eq. (<a href="#Pt0.A0.E33" title="Equation A33 ‣ VP-SDE with ϵ-Prediction. ‣ A.3 Weighted ℎ-Transform Inference for Various SDEs ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A33</span></a>):</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}-\lambda_{\sigma}\left(-\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}+\epsilon_{\theta}\right)=\epsilon_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}-\epsilon_{\theta}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}-\lambda_{\sigma}\left(-\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}+\epsilon_{\theta}\right)=\epsilon_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}-\epsilon_{\theta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This reveals the effective guided noise prediction <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}=\epsilon_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}-\epsilon_{\theta}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}=\epsilon_{\theta}+\lambda_{\sigma}\left(\widetilde{\bm{\epsilon}}-\epsilon_{\theta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the guided PF-ODE simplifies elegantly to the standard unguided formulation, driven entirely by the linearly interpolated noise <math id="Pt0.A0.SS3.SSSx2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A0.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A0.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)\mathrm{d}t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\frac{\dot{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}}\left(\bm{x}_{t}-\frac{\hat{\epsilon}_{\theta}}{\sigma_{t}}\right)\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Implementation details</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Obtaining the Coarse Videos.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Coarse-Video Guided Generation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Coarse-Guided Visual Generation via Weighted ℎ-Transform Sampling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we use 3-D models to render an image into a corresponding coarse warped video based on its camera intrinsics and poses. First, we leverage a pretrained depth estimation model, DepthPro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, to get the depth map of the first frame image. Then we reproject this depth map into a point cloud and render a sequence of images for given camera motion poses. To ensure motion quality, we filter out static or minimal-movement sequences where the camera translation extent is less than <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To resolve the scale ambiguity of monocular depth maps, we align them with the camera trajectories using SIFT feature matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> between the reference frame and subsequent frames (sampled at <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>-frame intervals). Matches are refined using a <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbor search (<math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>) and a Lowe’s ratio test threshold of <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.75</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.75</annotation></semantics></math>. After computing candidate scales via projection constraints, we discard the top and bottom <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\%</annotation></semantics></math> outliers and apply the median value as the final scale. The reference image is warped to target views by unprojecting valid pixels (depth &gt; <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) into 3-D space using the inverse intrinsic matrix and the calibrated depth. These points are transformed into the target camera coordinate system and splatted onto the 2-D image plane.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To correctly resolve self-occlusions during rendering, we implement a <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>-buffering approach by sorting the projected points in descending order of depth. To address deocclusion holes inherently caused by forward splatting, we implement a global nearest-neighbor filling strategy utilizing a k-d tree built on valid pixel coordinates. The corresponding visibility masks are further refined using morphological opening with a <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5*5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5*5</annotation></semantics></math> rectangular kernel to eliminate isolated projection noise and smooth edges. More details can be found in the code.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Image-to-Video Prompts Preparation.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For prompts generation, we follow the protocol of CogVideoX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, <em id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, leverage the pretrained Vision-Language model GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> to generate caption for the given first frame. These generated prompts will be used as the text condition for subsequent image-to-video generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The Implementation of Using Wan2.2 for Camera-controlled Video Generation.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Wan2.2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, we change the length and resolution of evaluated videos, <em id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, frame number from <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>49</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="81" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>81</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81</annotation></semantics></math> and the resolution from <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="720*480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>720</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>480</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">720*480</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="832*480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>832</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>480</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">832*480</annotation></semantics></math>. During sampling, we set the weight function <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\sigma}=\sigma^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\sigma}=\sigma^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and give these two parts different <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. For the valid part, <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=16</annotation></semantics></math> and for the invalid part, <math id="Pt0.A0.SS4.SSSx3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=20</annotation></semantics></math>.
For other hyperparameters of Wan2.2, we follow the implementations of TTM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A0.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Additional Results</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A0.SS5.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
